CORE
union_pointer_member.c

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ read through the union: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ type-punned read: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
Reading a pointer-typed union member through a pointer to the enclosing struct
rewrites the access as a typecast of the union's first member. Field
sensitivity must turn that member, not the typecast, into a field-sensitive
symbol, or the dereferenced pointer has no points-to set.
